cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Xdaptive in academic work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Xdaptive: an adaptive computing OS that generates, compiles and evolves software around intent"
abstract: >-
  Xdaptive is an operating system that treats the user's task, not the installed
  program, as the unit of computing. It interprets intent, composes the software
  a task needs into a single persistent Workspace, and adapts that Workspace in
  place when the task changes. The project's own technology is an intermediate
  representation (AIR) of software composition, a compiler that verifies and
  lowers it, an execution model that mutates running structure without losing
  state, and a Workspace runtime that owns lifecycle, versioning and recovery. A
  model may propose a plan; the OS validates, sandboxes and commits it, and
  rolls it back on failure.
type: software
